---
import Subscribe from '../components/Subscribe.astro';
import { LINKS } from '../consts';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="Hi, I'm Javlon, a solutions architect. Every week I test one thing engineers repeat and write down what I'd actually decide.">
	<div class="prose">
		<h1>About</h1>
		<div class="rule"></div>
		<p class="lead">Hi, I'm Javlon, a solutions architect at a food-delivery platform.</p>
		<p>
			For years I tried to write perfect code. Clean, clever, ready for every future. Most of that future never
			came. It took me too long to learn that architecture isn't about the perfect design. It's about a decision
			you can live with, and knowing what it costs.
		</p>
		<p>
			That's what Archemist is. Every week I take one thing engineers repeat ("Protobuf is faster", "extract the
			core service first"), test it with code you can run yourself, and write down what I'd actually decide.
		</p>
		<p>
			I'm not a guru. I read the books, break things on cheap cloud servers and share what survives. If I got
			something wrong, tell me. That's how this gets better.
		</p>

		<h2>What you'll find</h2>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Under the Hood</strong>: databases, encodings and data internals.</li>
			<li><strong>Architecture in Production</strong>: monoliths, services and the messy middle.</li>
			<li><strong>System Design</strong>: judgment calls and what breaks after the whiteboard.</li>
			<li><strong>AI Engineering</strong>: AI systems and tools, judged by an architect.</li>
			<li><strong>Career</strong>: seniority, growth paths and how architects work.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>Tests you can re-run</h2>
		<p>
			Every number in an article comes from a script in the <a href={LINKS.github}>labs repository</a>: pinned
			dependencies, synthetic data, run on a named cloud server. Clone it and check the results yourself.
		</p>

		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>
			<a href={LINKS.email}>hello@archemist.dev</a>. Short videos in English on YouTube; the same diagrams in Uzbek
			and Russian on Telegram.
		</p>

		<Subscribe />
	</div>
</Base>

<style>
	.prose {
		max-width: var(--measure);
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding-top: 1.5rem;
	}
	.lead {
		font-size: 1.15rem;
	}
</style>
